{"packet_id":"D043-01","doc_id":"D043","jurisdiction":"Los Angeles, CA","category":"just_cause_eviction","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"No-fault eviction relocation and declaration requirement","requirement":"Before evicting tenants from an RSO- or JCO-covered unit for a no-fault reason, a landlord must file a Declaration of Intent to Evict with LAHD and pay relocation assistance; the notice may be served only after filing.","key_value":"Declaration filed before notice served; notice copy within 3 days","coverage_conditions":"Units covered by the Rent Stabilization Ordinance (RSO) or the Just Cause Ordinance (JCO).","applicability":{"built_on_or_before":null,"built_after":null,"date_basis":null,"min_units":null,"max_units":null,"owner_dependent":false,"other":"RSO- or JCO-covered rental units"},"exemptions":null,"penalty":"Failure to file the Landlord Declaration with LAHD makes the eviction a violation of the RSO or JCO.","effective_date":null,"citation":"L.A. Mun. Code § 151.09","quoted_span":"All tenant not- at-fault evictions require payment of relocation assistance and the filing of a Declaration of Intent to Evict form with the Los Angeles Housing Department (LAHD) before evicting tenants from units covered by the Rent Stabilization Ordinance (RSO) or the Just Cause Ordinance (JCO).","interaction":null,"confidence":0.8,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D043-01","doc_id":"D043","jurisdiction":"Los Angeles, CA","category":"just_cause_eviction","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"RSO/JCO relocation assistance amounts (2026-2027)","requirement":"A landlord displacing a tenant for a no-fault reason must pay the Chart A relocation amount: $11,000 or $14,400 for an eligible tenant and $23,150 or $27,400 for a qualified tenant, based on length of tenancy.","key_value":"Eligible $11,000 (<3 yrs) / $14,400 (3+ yrs); Qualified $23,150 / $27,400; 2026-07-01 to 2027-06-30","coverage_conditions":"Tenants displaced for a no-fault reason described in the bulletin under the RSO or JCO; amounts increase every July 1.","applicability":{"built_on_or_before":null,"built_after":null,"date_basis":null,"min_units":null,"max_units":null,"owner_dependent":false,"other":"RSO/JCO no-fault displacement"},"exemptions":null,"penalty":null,"effective_date":"2026-07-01","citation":"A. Relocation Assistance Bulletin, Chart A","quoted_span":"Eligible Tenant $11,000 $14,400 Qualified Tenant $23,150 $27,400","interaction":null,"confidence":0.8,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D043-01","doc_id":"D043","jurisdiction":"Los Angeles, CA","category":"just_cause_eviction","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Relocation assistance payment deadline","requirement":"Relocation assistance must be made available within 15 days of service of the written notice of eviction, or placed in an escrow account within that period at the landlord's cost.","key_value":"15 days from service of notice","coverage_conditions":"No-fault evictions of units covered by the RSO or JCO.","applicability":{"built_on_or_before":null,"built_after":null,"date_basis":null,"min_units":null,"max_units":null,"owner_dependent":false,"other":"RSO/JCO no-fault displacement"},"exemptions":null,"penalty":null,"effective_date":null,"citation":"A. Relocation Assistance Bulletin (Relocation payment timing)","quoted_span":"Payment shall be made available within fifteen (15) days of service of the written notice of eviction","interaction":null,"confidence":0.8,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D043-01","doc_id":"D043","jurisdiction":"Los Angeles, CA","category":"just_cause_eviction","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Mom and Pop reduced relocation assistance","requirement":"Mom and Pop landlords may pay reduced relocation assistance for a good-faith eviction for owner, family or manager occupancy only if the building has four or fewer rental units and the other LAMC § 151.30 conditions are met.","key_value":null,"coverage_conditions":"Mom and Pop properties with four or fewer rental units; landlord used no such provision in the prior three years and owns no more than four units plus a single-family home.","applicability":{"built_on_or_before":null,"built_after":null,"date_basis":null,"min_units":null,"max_units":4,"owner_dependent":true,"other":"Mom and Pop owner-occupancy eviction"},"exemptions":null,"penalty":null,"effective_date":null,"citation":"L.A. Mun. Code § 151.30","quoted_span":"Mom and Pop properties may pay reduced relocation assistance payments to their tenants for a good faith eviction for occupancy by the owner or eligible relative, provided that requirements  in Section 151.30 of the LAMC are met.","interaction":null,"confidence":0.8,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D043-01","doc_id":"D043","jurisdiction":"Los Angeles, CA","category":"just_cause_eviction","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Single-family JCO relocation: one month's rent","requirement":"Where a JCO-covered single-family dwelling is owned by a natural person who owns no more than four dwelling units plus a single-family home on a separate lot, relocation is one month's rent in effect when notice was served.","key_value":"1 month's rent","coverage_conditions":"Single-family dwelling subject to the JCO owned by a natural person (including trusts or controlled entities) owning no more than four dwelling units and a single-family home on a separate lot in Los Angeles.","applicability":{"built_on_or_before":null,"built_after":null,"date_basis":null,"min_units":null,"max_units":4,"owner_dependent":true,"other":"Single-family dwelling owned by a natural person"},"exemptions":"The Los Angeles Municipal Code Section 151.30(E) shall not apply.","penalty":null,"effective_date":null,"citation":"L.A. Mun. Code § 165.06","quoted_span":"the owner is a natural person, including natural  persons who hold properties in a trust or registered legal entity controlled by   that natural person, who owns no more than four dwelling units and a single-family home on a separate lot  in the City of Los Angeles: one month’s rent that was in effect when   the landlord served the written notice to terminate the tenancy, as either a monetary payment or credit.","interaction":null,"confidence":0.8,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D043-01","doc_id":"D043","jurisdiction":"Los Angeles, CA","category":"just_cause_eviction","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Exemptions from relocation assistance payments","requirement":"A landlord need not pay relocation assistance when replacing a resident manager, when a required eviction stems from hazardous conditions from a natural disaster not caused by landlord negligence, or by offsetting the tenant's accumulated rent.","key_value":null,"coverage_conditions":"Relocation assistance obligations for no-fault evictions under the RSO and JCO.","applicability":{"built_on_or_before":null,"built_after":null,"date_basis":null,"min_units":null,"max_units":null,"owner_dependent":false,"other":"RSO/JCO relocation assistance"},"exemptions":"Replacing a resident manager; required eviction due to hazardous conditions from a natural disaster not caused by landlord negligence; offset of accumulated rent (LAMC 151.09.G,5., 165.06.J.).","penalty":null,"effective_date":null,"citation":"L.A. Mun. Code § 151.09","quoted_span":"Relocation Offset: A landlord may offset the tenant's accumulated rent against any relocation assistance, unless the relocation assistance is owed because a termination of tenancy is required by a governmental agency order to vacate or comply with an issued order for an unpermitted dwelling.","interaction":null,"confidence":0.8,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D043-01","doc_id":"D043","jurisdiction":"Los Angeles, CA","category":"just_cause_eviction","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Tenant remedy for non-payment of relocation assistance","requirement":"A tenant may raise the landlord's failure to provide relocation assistance as an affirmative defense in an eviction action and may file a complaint with LAHD.","key_value":null,"coverage_conditions":"Tenants in RSO- or JCO-covered units facing a no-fault eviction.","applicability":{"built_on_or_before":null,"built_after":null,"date_basis":null,"min_units":null,"max_units":null,"owner_dependent":false,"other":"RSO/JCO no-fault eviction"},"exemptions":null,"penalty":null,"effective_date":null,"citation":"A. Relocation Assistance Bulletin (Tenant remedies)","quoted_span":"In an action by the landlord to recover possession of a rental unit, the tenant may raise as an affirmative defense the failure of the landlord to provide relocation assistance.","interaction":null,"confidence":0.8,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D043-01","doc_id":"D043","jurisdiction":"Los Angeles, CA","category":"just_cause_eviction","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Resident Protections Ordinance relocation compliance","requirement":"An owner who demolishes a Protected Unit for new construction within 5 years after filing the notice must comply with RPO relocation requirements, paying the higher of State HCA or City law amounts, enhanced for lower income tenants.","key_value":"Penalties start at $250,000 per displaced unit","coverage_conditions":"Protected Units demolished for new construction within 5 years after filing the Notice of Intent to Withdraw or Declaration of Intent to Evict.","applicability":{"built_on_or_before":null,"built_after":null,"date_basis":null,"min_units":null,"max_units":null,"owner_dependent":false,"other":"Protected Units demolished for new construction"},"exemptions":null,"penalty":"Financial penalties starting at $250,000 per displaced unit and withholding of LAHD permit clearances.","effective_date":"2025-02-11","citation":"Ordinances #188481, #188482","quoted_span":"Failure to comply with the RPO may result in financial penalties starting at $250,000 per displaced unit and withholding of LAHD permit clearances.","interaction":"Owner must pay the higher of State Housing Crisis Act or City relocation amounts.","confidence":0.8,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
